  <h2>When a logo is required vs when a GBP fix is enough</h2>
  <p>
    If the profile category, photos, and basics are wrong, fix Google first. That alone can get
    calls moving again without a rebrand. If you’re already booking work (or launching with real intent to scale), brand
    becomes the foundation everything else sits on: vans, uniforms, site, ads, referrals. Dan
    Interdelli’s <em>Branded Not Blended</em> argument holds: earlier is cheaper than ripping and
    replacing once people already know you as “the decent guys,” not a distinct company.
  </p>
  <p>
    Branding is the same discipline as the rest of marketing: competition, customer desire, clarity,
    not “what looks cool in the shop.” We design for the homeowner’s doorstep, then carry that
    system into the website and Google profile so the market sees one company.
  </p>
